    {
      "id": "cn7Aepqh3-lDWaLRtiU_e",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 316.9499206542969,
      "y": 1521.4999694824219,
      "width": 997.639404296875,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1011847386,
      "version": 1150,
      "versionNonce": 769521222,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779304558956,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- During component scan may be we need some dependency, Spring says, I know how to \ncreate objects of these classes, so I can automatically inject them for you.\n\n- @Autowired : using this annotation we can do field based dependency injection, with latest \nversion of SpringBoot this is discouraged to use\nConstructor based injection is preferred due to the fact that we can't use final in field injection\nand using final is very important because without that there will be a risk of change of object during \nthe runtime.\n\n\n- In some situations it wont be trivial for spring to create the objects of your classes, in those\ncases we have to give a manual implementation that spring will invoke whenever it needs those kind\nof objects. And this situation introduce another annotation ie @Bean\n \n\n\n\n@Qualifier\n@Primary\n@Value\n@ConfigurationProperties\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- During component scan may be we need some dependency, Spring says, I know how to \ncreate objects of these classes, so I can automatically inject them for you.\n\n- @Autowired : using this annotation we can do field based dependency injection, with latest \nversion of SpringBoot this is discouraged to use\nConstructor based injection is preferred due to the fact that we can't use final in field injection\nand using final is very important because without that there will be a risk of change of object during \nthe runtime.\n\n\n- In some situations it wont be trivial for spring to create the objects of your classes, in those\ncases we have to give a manual implementation that spring will invoke whenever it needs those kind\nof objects. And this situation introduce another annotation ie @Bean\n \n\n\n\n@Qualifier\n@Primary\n@Value\n@ConfigurationProperties\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
